<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korean bank union postpones strike.</title>
<headline>South Korean bank union postpones strike.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Korean Federation of Bank and Financial Workers' Unions on Tuesday called on members to postpone a strike planned for Saturday, a union official said.</p>
<p>The move follows a call by the umbrella Federation of Korean Trade Unions to suspend industrial action until January 11, bank union official Kong Kwang-kyu said.  </p>
<p>&quot;We will delay our plans until the federation calls on us to start the work stoppage,&quot; Kong said.</p>
<p>The strikes are in protest at a controversial labour law railroaded through parliament last week that allows companies to lay off workers and replace strikers.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
